{"name":"Farm House","hex":"#eee8d6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"farm house","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of farmhouse."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/farm_house"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Farm House (Knapp–Wilson House)","blocks":[{"text":"The Farm House, also known as the Knapp–Wilson House, is the oldest building on the campus of Iowa State University in Ames, Iowa. Now a museum open to the general public, this house was originally built in 1860 as part of the model farm aspect of Iowa Agricultural College and Model Farm. It was designated a National Historic Landmark in 1965 for its association with agriculturist Seaman A. Knapp and U.S. Secretary of Agriculture James Wilson, both of whom lived here while teaching at Iowa State."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/The_Farm_House_ISU.jpg/330px-The_Farm_House_ISU.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Farm_House_(Knapp%E2%80%93Wilson_House)"},{"title":"Farmhouse","blocks":[{"text":"A farmhouse is a building that serves as the primary quarters in a rural or agricultural setting. Historically, farmhouses were often combined with space for animals called a housebarn. Other farmhouses may be connected to one or more barns, built to form a courtyard, or with each farm building separate from each other."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Einsiedeln_IMG_2819.JPG/330px-Einsiedeln_IMG_2819.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farmhouse"},{"title":"Farm","blocks":[{"text":"A farm is an area of land that is devoted primarily to agricultural processes with the primary objective of producing food and other crops; it is the basic facility in food production. The name is used for specialized units such as arable farms, vegetable farms, fruit farms, dairy, pig and poultry farms, and land used for the production of natural fiber, biofuel, and other biobased products. It includes ranches, feedlots, orchards, plantations and estates, smallholdings, and hobby farms, and includes the farmhouse and agricultural buildings as well as the land. In modern times, the term has been extended to include such industrial operations as wind farms and fish farms, both of which can operate on land or at sea."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Church_Farm%2C_Stockton%2C_Norfolk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1968544.jpg/330px-Church_Farm%2C_Stockton%2C_Norfolk_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1968544.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farm"},{"title":"House","blocks":[{"text":"A house is a residential building. It may range in complexity from a rudimentary hut to a complex structure of wood, masonry, concrete or other material, outfitted with plumbing, electrical, and heating, ventilation, and air conditioning systems. Houses use a range of different roofing systems to keep precipitation such as rain from getting into the dwelling space. Houses generally have doors or locks to secure the dwelling space and protect its inhabitants and contents from burglars or other trespassers. Most conventional modern houses in Western cultures will contain one or more bedrooms and bathrooms, a kitchen or cooking area, and a living room. A house may have a separate dining room, or the eating area may be integrated into the kitchen or another room. Some large houses in North America have a recreation room. In traditional agriculture-oriented societies, domestic animals such as chickens or larger livestock may share part of the house with humans."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg/330px-Katsura_Imperial_Villa_in_Spring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/House"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg/500px-The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg/1280px-The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg/500px-The_Farm_House_%28Knapp-Wilson_House%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Farm House in the early 20th Century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Farm_House_(Knapp-Wilson_House).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/500px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/1280px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg/500px-The_Devil%27s_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Devil's Farmhouse in Mellieħa, Malta, built by the Order of St. John with limestone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Devil's_Farmhouse_in_Mellieha%2C_Malta.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg/250px-Farmhouse_upper_Trenta_Soca_06052006_63.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&